│ article constitute the co-ordinating team.Citeseer"}, {"study_index": 80, "title": "Transjugular liver biopsy ‐      │
│ indications, adequacy, quality of specimens, and complications ‐ a systematic review", "abstract": "Transjugular     │
│ liver biopsy (TJLB) is considered an inferior biopsy, used when percutaneous liver biopsy (PLB) is contraindicated.  │
│ According to recent literature, specimens with 6 complete portal tracts (CPTs) are needed for histological diagnosis │
