│ Eighty-three evaluable patients undergoing valvular heart operations were randomized to receive desmopressin (0.3    │
│ microgram/kg) (41) or placebo (42) after cardiac bypass. Demographic characteristics were similar in both groups.    │
│ There was no significant difference in total 24-hour blood loss between groups (desmopressin 1064.8 +/- 647.1 ml     │
│ versus placebo 844.4 +/- 507.6 ml; p greater than 0.05), or in the requirement for red blood cell, platelet, or      │
│ fresh frozen plasma transfusion, or for reexploration for control of hemorrhage. Neither was there a difference in   │
